# What must NOT be published.
#
# vercel.json sets outputDirectory to ".", so before this file existed the whole
# repository was served from the public domain. Verified on production:
# docs/STATUS.md, docs/OWNER-MANUAL-STEPS.md, AGENTS.md, scripts/*.mjs and
# supabase/migrations/0001_init_schema.sql all returned 200. STATUS.md describes
# the three past credential incidents in detail, names the Supabase project, and
# states plainly that sign-in is enforced in the browser only and can be
# bypassed. That is a map for anyone who thinks to look.
#
# None of it is a live credential — the keys live in Vercel's environment, not
# in the repo — and nothing here is deleted. It simply stops being published.

# Working documents and process
docs/
*.md
!api/**/*.md
.github/
.githooks/
.vscode/
.cursorrules
.mcp.json

# Test and tooling source.
# `scripts/*` rather than `scripts/` deliberately: gitignore semantics do not
# allow re-including a file whose parent directory is excluded, and the build
# needs exactly one file out of here. Excluding the contents instead leaves the
# negation below able to work. stamp-version.mjs holds no secrets — it reads two
# environment variables and writes version.json.
scripts/*
!scripts/stamp-version.mjs
evidence/

# Database schema and migrations
supabase/

# Superseded material
legacy/

# Local environment
.env
.env.*
node_modules/
